IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tla-title`

-- Transfer of Land Act 1893 (WA), ss 52(2), 53, 58, 60, 61, 68, 105-108, 187, 199, 201, 214A, 227 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_transfer-of-land-act-1893.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*/facts.json and SCENARIO.md): Chloe (25) and Liam (28) settle
-- the Byford land on 2028-05-15 and "the mortgage is registered on a Torrens title" (c052); the Baldivis townhouse in a community
-- titles scheme, $1,300,000, 2040-04-28 (c081); Jake (38) settles his strata apartment 2045-03-20 (k076); Graham and Sue hold the
-- Armadale house "as joint tenants"; Graham dies 2052-08-19 with a will naming Chloe executor, Sue 79 (c087); Liam dies
-- 2083-02-09, "the apartment by survivorship" to Chloe, 79 (c096); Giuseppe dies 2052-11-03 owning a house in Reggio Calabria
-- (d074); Daniel dies, "the house to Priya by survivorship", Priya 81, 2078-11-15 (d093). The scenarios do not say how Chloe and
-- Liam, or Daniel and Priya, are registered; joint proprietorship is ASSUMED where a life says "by survivorship". The
-- signatures on the Byford mortgage are assumed.

§ `Fixtures`

`Chloe and Liam's Byford mortgage, registered at settlement on 2028-05-15` MEANS Mortgage WITH
    `registered` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the mortgagee` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the proprietor of the land` IS TRUE
    `the proprietor of the land signed a counterpart before registration` IS TRUE

`a mortgage lodged with only the lender's counterpart, the owners having signed one before registration` MEANS Mortgage WITH
    `registered` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the mortgagee` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `the proprietor of the land signed a counterpart before registration` IS TRUE

`a mortgage lodged with only the lender's counterpart, the owners never having signed` MEANS Mortgage WITH
    `registered` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the mortgagee` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the proprietor of the land` IS FALSE
    `the proprietor of the land signed a counterpart before registration` IS FALSE

`a mortgage signed by everyone but never registered` MEANS Mortgage WITH
    `registered` IS FALSE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the mortgagee` IS TRUE
    `a lodged counterpart is signed by the proprietor of the land` IS TRUE
    `the proprietor of the land signed a counterpart before registration` IS TRUE

§ `ss 52(2), 58 and 53 -- registration and priority`

-- c052: the transfer to Chloe and Liam passes the land when, and only when, its memorandum is entered on the certificate.
#ASSERT `the instrument passes the estate or interest` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the instrument passes the estate or interest` FALSE

-- s 53(2): a mortgage dated first but registered second is second.
#ASSERT `the first instrument has priority` 1 2
#ASSERT NOT `the first instrument has priority` 2 1

§ `ss 68 and 134 -- paramountcy and its exceptions (c052, c081, k076)`

#ASSERT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `an encumbrance notified on the certificate`
#ASSERT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `the estate of a proprietor under a prior registered certificate for the same land`
#ASSERT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `unpaid rates`
#ASSERT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `an easement acquired by enjoyment or user`
#ASSERT NOT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `an unregistered mortgage`
#ASSERT NOT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `an unregistered interest the proprietor knew of`
#ASSERT NOT `the interest binds the registered proprietor despite section 68` `a trust not entered on the certificate`

#ASSERT `section 68 frees the registered proprietor from the interest` `an unregistered mortgage` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 68 frees the registered proprietor from the interest` `an unregistered mortgage` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 68 frees the registered proprietor from the interest` `unpaid rates` FALSE

-- prior unregistered lease: registered, prior, term in years, tenant in actual possession
#ASSERT `the registered proprietor takes subject to the lease` FALSE TRUE 5 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the registered proprietor takes subject to the lease` FALSE TRUE 6 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the registered proprietor takes subject to the lease` FALSE TRUE 1 FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `an option in the lease is valid against a later registered interest` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `an option in the lease is valid against a later registered interest` FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `section 68 protects land included by wrong description` FALSE

§ `ss 199, 201, 214A -- recovery, compensation, fraud`

#ASSERT `an action to recover the land lies against the registered proprietor` `a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default`
#ASSERT `an action to recover the land lies against the registered proprietor` `a person deprived by fraud against the proprietor registered through that fraud`
#ASSERT NOT `an action to recover the land lies against the registered proprietor` `a person deprived by fraud against a later transferee bona fide for value`
#ASSERT NOT `an action to recover the land lies against the registered proprietor` `a misdescription claimant against a bona fide transferee for value`
#ASSERT NOT `an action to recover the land lies against the registered proprietor` `a person with an unregistered interest`

-- deprived, dead, bankrupt, not found, liability capped by a bona fide transfer
#ASSERT `damages may be recovered from the State` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `damages may be recovered from the State` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `damages may be recovered from the State` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `the certificate or instrument is void against the person` TRUE FALSE

§ `ss 105, 105AA, 106 -- what the lender registers (c052)`

#ASSERT `the mortgage binds the proprietor of the land` `Chloe and Liam's Byford mortgage, registered at settlement on 2028-05-15`
#ASSERT `the mortgage binds the proprietor of the land` `a mortgage lodged with only the lender's counterpart, the owners having signed one before registration`
#ASSERT NOT `the mortgage binds the proprietor of the land` `a mortgage lodged with only the lender's counterpart, the owners never having signed`
#ASSERT NOT `the mortgage binds the proprietor of the land` `a mortgage signed by everyone but never registered`

#ASSERT `the mortgage may be lodged electronically` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the mortgage may be lodged electronically` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `a registered mortgage operates as` `a security over the land`
#ASSERT NOT `a registered mortgage operates as` `a transfer of the land`

§ `ss 106, 107, 108 -- default and sale`

#ASSERT `months the default must continue` 0 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `months the default must continue` 3 EQUALS 3

#ASSERT `the mortgagee may serve a notice to pay` TRUE 1 0
#ASSERT NOT `the mortgagee may serve a notice to pay` TRUE 1 2

#ASSERT `the notice is properly served` `left in a conspicuous place on the land`
#ASSERT NOT `the notice is properly served` `ordinary post`

-- on demand, demand made, method, notice served, months after notice or demand, months fixed for sale
#ASSERT `the mortgagee may sell the land` FALSE FALSE `registered post to the address in the Register` TRUE 1 0
#ASSERT NOT `the mortgagee may sell the land` FALSE FALSE `ordinary post` TRUE 2 0
#ASSERT `the mortgagee may sell the land` TRUE TRUE `ordinary post` FALSE 1 0

§ `ss 60, 61 -- joint proprietors (c087, c096, d093)`

#ASSERT `the proprietors are deemed joint tenants` `as joint proprietors` 2
#ASSERT NOT `the proprietors are deemed joint tenants` `as joint proprietors` 1
#ASSERT NOT `the proprietors are deemed joint tenants` `as tenants in common in undivided shares` 2

#ASSERT `separate certificates may issue for undivided shares` `as tenants in common in undivided shares`

#ASSERT NOT `the person may lawfully deal with the property` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the person may lawfully deal with the property` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `ss 227, 187 -- after a death`

-- registered under the Act, holding, applicant is the person entitled, death proved
-- c087 Sue after Graham; c096 Chloe after Liam; d093 Priya after Daniel (all joint, assumed or stated): no probate needed.
-- d074 the Reggio Calabria house is not registered under this Act. A sole proprietor's land does not go by s 227.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner may direct the survivor's registration under section 227` TRUE `as joint proprietors` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Commissioner may direct the survivor's registration under section 227` FALSE `as sole proprietor` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Commissioner may direct the survivor's registration under section 227` TRUE `as sole proprietor` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Commissioner may direct the survivor's registration under section 227` TRUE `as joint proprietors` TRUE FALSE

#ASSERT `the Registrar must register the legal personal representative under section 187` TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `the representatives may deal with the land` 2 1

